    tags: [
      "tko airraid runner manual treadmill 8ctm",
      "tko airraid runner",
      "tko 8ctm",
      "tko airraid force",
      "tko curved treadmill",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "See Who It Suits", link: "#who-it-suits" }}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <svg class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full opacity-10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <pattern id="dot-pattern-tkoairraidrunnertreadmill" x="0" y="0" width="24" height="24" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
          <circle cx="2" cy="2" r="1.5" fill="white"></circle>
        </pattern>
        <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#dot-pattern-tkoairraidrunnertreadmill)"></rect>
      </svg>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3 mb-6 flex-wrap">
          <span class="bg-[#FF5A1F] text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Model Review
          </span>
          <span class="bg-green-500 text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Updated October 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          TKO AirRaid Runner 8CTM <span class="text-[#5AA9FF]">Manual Treadmill Review</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          The TKO AirRaid Runner 8CTM is a commercial curved manual treadmill with four magnetic resistance levels and Zwift-compatible Bluetooth. TKO now sells it as the AirRaid Force, and has given the AirRaid Runner name to a different machine. This review sorts out which is which, what TKO and its dealers confirm, where the figures conflict, and who should buy it.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
          <a href="#which-model" class="bg-[#FF5A1F] hover:bg-[#E64F16] text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
            Which Model Is Which
          </a>
          <a href="#who-it-suits" class="bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm border border-white/20">
            Who Should Buy It
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 py-8 border-b border-gray-100">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="48" height="48" class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full" />
        <div>
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight"><a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author" class="text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a></p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm leading-tight">Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block w-px h-8 bg-gray-200"></div>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm">
          Last Updated: <strong class="text-gray-700">October 14, 2026</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="1.2k" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose my-10 bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 m-0 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          14 October 2026 we read TKO Strength &amp; Performance's own product pages for the AirRaid
          Force (SKU 8CTM-B) and the AirRaid Runner (8CRUN), TKO's sell sheets for both dated 13 May
          2026, the 8CTM-B owner's manual, and TKO's return policy, and compared them with four US dealer
          listings for the 8CTM (Select Fitness, Push Pedal Pull, Iron Company and The Fitness Outlet).
          TKO's sell sheet and the dealers agree on the 68 x 32 x 67 in. footprint, the 350 lb maximum
          user weight, four-level magnetic resistance, ANT+ and Bluetooth, and a 5-year frame and 2-year
          parts warranty. They disagree on machine weight (297 lb on TKO's sheet and two dealers, 330 lb
          on two others). The 63 x 17.3 in. running surface appears only on dealer listings, and TKO's
          manual gives different figures for surface, dimensions, capacity, slat count and warranty; we
          state each as a conflict rather than choosing. We found no independent hands-on review or
          owner report. We have not tested the 8CTM. Prices and stock were as shown on 14 October 2026
          and change often. We earn a commission if you buy through the Amazon link on this page; it
          does not change what we say about the machine.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mt-0 mb-4">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-[#FF5A1F]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h7"></path></svg>
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#short-answer" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">1. TKO AirRaid Runner Manual Treadmill 8CTM: The Short Answer</a>
          <a href="#which-model" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">2. AirRaid Runner, AirRaid Force, 8CTM and 8CRUN: Which Is Which</a>
          <a href="#specifications" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">3. The 8CTM Specifications, and Where They Conflict</a>
          <a href="#how-it-trains" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">4. How a Curved Treadmill With Magnetic Resistance Trains</a>
          <a href="#console-and-apps" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">5. The Console, Zwift and Kinomap</a>
          <a href="#warranty-and-returns" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">6. Warranty, Returns and Delivery</a>
          <a href="#who-it-suits" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">7. Who It Suits, and What to Consider Instead</a>
          <a href="#verdict" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">8. The Verdict</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">9. Frequently Asked Questions</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Search for the TKO AirRaid Runner manual treadmill 8CTM and you will find dealers selling it
          under that name at around $5,000 to $5,500. Go to TKO's own site and the 8CTM is listed as the
          TKO AirRaid Force, while "AirRaid Runner" now belongs to a newer model, the 8CRUN, with no
          resistance system and different figures. Both are real, both are curved and self-powered, and
          they are easy to confuse. This page is about the 8CTM. It sets out what TKO's own sell sheet
          confirms, where TKO's manual and dealer listings disagree with it, how a curved treadmill with
          magnetic resistance trains, and who it suits — with the 8CRUN covered where it matters.
        </p>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">1. TKO AirRaid Runner Manual Treadmill 8CTM: The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>The TKO AirRaid Runner manual treadmill 8CTM is a current, commercial-grade curved
            treadmill with four magnetic resistance levels, a 350 lb rating on TKO's sell sheet and
            Zwift-compatible Bluetooth, sold for about $5,000 to $5,500 — and TKO itself now lists it as
            the AirRaid Force.</strong> It is a reasonable buy for a facility or committed athlete who
            wants resistance and connectivity on a curved belt. For most home buyers, it costs a lot more
            than curved treadmills that do similar things.
          </p>
          <p>
            Three things to know before you buy. First, check the model number: TKO's current "AirRaid
            Runner" is the 8CRUN, a different machine with no resistance system. Second, several figures
            are not settled — TKO's sell sheet, its owner's manual and dealer listings give different
            machine weights, running surfaces, capacities and warranty terms. Third, we found no
            independent review or owner report of the 8CTM, so its figures are TKO's and its dealers'
            claims rather than anything measured.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you are comparing curved treadmills, our
            <a href="/best-curved-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best curved treadmills</a>
            roundup covers the better-documented options, and our
            <a href="/assaultrunner-pro-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">AssaultRunner Pro review</a>
            covers the machine most buyers will set this one against. If you are still deciding whether a
            curved, self-powered treadmill suits you, start with our
            <a href="/curved-treadmill-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">curved treadmill guide</a>.
            We have not tested the 8CTM.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Product cards -->
      <div class="not-prose">
        {
          PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <div id={product.id} class="scroll-mt-24 mt-12 first:mt-8">
              <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm">
                <div class="bg-gray-900 px-6 py-4 flex items-center justify-between flex-wrap gap-3">
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="text-white font-black text-xl leading-tight m-0">
                      {index + 1}. {product.name}
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs">{product.category}</p>
                  </div>
                  <span class="bg-[#FF5A1F] text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
                    {product.badge}
                  </span>
                </div>
                <div class="p-6">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 flex-wrap">
                    <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400">Typical street price</span>
                    <span class="ml-auto font-black text-gray-900">{product.priceRange}</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 mb-4">{product.specs}</p>
                  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6" set:html={product.description} />
                  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
                    <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-100 rounded-xl p-4">
                      <h4 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-green-700 mt-0 mb-2">What We Like</h4>
                      <ul class="space-y-2">
                        {product.pros.map((pro) => (
                          <li class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">{pro}</li>
                        ))}
                      </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-xl p-4">
                      <h4 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-red-700 mt-0 mb-2">What We Don't Like</h4>
                      <ul class="space-y-2">
                        {product.cons.map((con) => (
                          <li class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">{con}</li>
                        ))}
                      </ul>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="border-t border-gray-100 pt-4">
                    <p class="text-gray-900 font-bold mb-4">{product.bottomLine}</p>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
                      <a href={product.amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="bg-[#FF5A1F] hover:bg-[#E64F16] text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
                        {product.amazonLabel} &rarr;
                      </a>
                      {product.reviewUrl && (
                        <a href={product.reviewUrl} class="text-[#0F62FE] font-bold no-underline text-sm hover:underline">
                          Read our full {product.name} review &rarr;
                        </a>
                      )}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <div id="which-model" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">2. AirRaid Runner, AirRaid Force, 8CTM and 8CRUN: Which Is Which</h2>
<p>
            TKO Strength &amp; Performance is a commercial fitness equipment company based in Houston,
            Texas, whose cardio line is aimed, in its own words, at high-traffic facilities such as health
            clubs, universities and high schools. Its AirRaid range includes an air bike, a rower, a ski
            trainer and two curved treadmills. The treadmills are where the confusion starts.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>8CTM / 8CTM-B — the machine on this page.</strong> Long sold by dealers as the
            "TKO AirRaid Runner" or "AirRaid Runner Curved Self-Powered Treadmill (8CTM)". TKO's own site
            now lists it as the <strong>TKO AirRaid Force</strong>, SKU 8CTM-B, at $5,500, and its May 2026
            sell sheet is headed "TKO AirRaid Force Runner". It has four-level magnetic resistance.</li>
            <li><strong>8CRUN — the new AirRaid Runner.</strong> TKO's site lists a separate "TKO AirRaid
            Runner" at $5,850, on a request-a-quote basis. Its sell sheet gives a 61 by 17-inch running
            surface, a 400 lb maximum user weight, a 290 lb net weight, overall dimensions of 72 by 33.5
            by 66.5 inches, an 8.6-inch LCD powered by three AA batteries, Bluetooth and ANT+, 100
            precision ball bearings with 12 roller guides, and a warranty of 10 years on the frame, 3 on
            parts and 1 on wear items and labour. Neither its product page nor its sell sheet lists a
            resistance system.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            In practice, a dealer page titled "AirRaid Runner" with four-level magnetic resistance, a
            68 by 32 by 67-inch footprint and a 350 lb rating is the 8CTM. A page with a 400 lb rating and
            a 61 by 17-inch surface is the 8CRUN. The Fitness Outlet sells the 8CTM-B under the AirRaid
            Force name and says neither model is a strict upgrade over the other, which is a fair summary:
            the 8CTM offers resistance, the 8CRUN a higher rating and a longer frame warranty. Put the
            model number on your order and your invoice, because the two have different warranties.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Where the 8CTM is sold in the US</h3>
          <p>
            On 14 October 2026 we found the 8CTM listed at:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>TKO (direct):</strong> as the AirRaid Force, $5,500, available to add to cart.</li>
            <li><strong>Select Fitness:</strong> as the "TKO 8CTM AirRaid Runner", $5,000 against
            $5,500, shipping in about 3–5 business days.</li>
            <li><strong>The Fitness Outlet:</strong> as the AirRaid Force (8CTM-B), $5,000 against
            $5,500, with an estimated 6–10 day delivery.</li>
            <li><strong>Push Pedal Pull:</strong> as the "TKO AirRaid Runner Treadmill", $5,500.</li>
            <li><strong>Iron Company:</strong> as the "AirRaid Runner Curved Self-Powered Treadmill
            (8CTM)", marked available, price on request at checkout.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We found no Amazon listing for it. Because TKO sells mainly through commercial dealers, it is
            worth asking two or three for a quote, especially if you are equipping a facility.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="specifications" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">3. The 8CTM Specifications, and Where They Conflict</h2>
<p>
            TKO's own documents do not fully agree with each other. Its May 2026 sell sheet and product
            page give one set of figures; the owner's manual, a generic document headed "Force", gives
            another. Dealer listings mostly follow the sell sheet but add a running surface TKO's sheet
            does not state. The table shows each figure and how settled it is.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[520px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Item</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">TKO sell sheet / product page</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Other sources</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Overall size</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">68 x 32 x 67 in</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">All four dealers agree; manual gives 1940 x 930 x 1685 mm (about 76 x 37 x 66 in)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Machine weight</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">297 lb</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">297 lb (Select Fitness, Push Pedal Pull); 330 lb (Iron Company, The Fitness Outlet)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Max user weight</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">350 lb</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">All four dealers agree; manual gives 150 kg (about 330 lb)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Running surface</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not stated</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">63 x 17.3 in (three dealers); manual gives 1660 x 440 mm (about 65.4 x 17.3 in)</td></tr>
